-- title:
--   All-edges Exact Triangle in time $O(\kappa\, n^{3-143/68400}\log^2 n)$ from the pruned Lop detection
-- statement:
--   Assume Lop-AE-SparseTri detection has the running time of the thin regime, that is, $\mathrm{LopDetectP}$ holds: for some $C\ge0$ the problem is solved in a time $T_d$ with
--   $$T_d(n,D,w)\le C\Big(\frac{n^2\log^2D}{D^{0.07618}}+w\,D^{0.44274}\log D+nD+w+1\Big)\quad\text{whenever }D\ge2,\ D^{91}\le n^5 .$$
--   Then All-Edges Exact Triangle is solved, uniformly in the size and the weights, in time
--   $$T(s,u)=K\,s^{\,3-143/68400}\,(\log s+1)^2\,(1+\log\max(u,2))^2$$
--   for some constant $K\ge1$, where $s$ is the number of vertices per part and $u$ an upper bound on the absolute values of the weights.
--
--   Here All-Edges Exact Triangle asks, given integer weight matrices $w_{AB},w_{BC},w_{AC}\in\mathbb Z^{s\times s}$, for the flag of every pair $(a,b)$ telling whether some $c$ has $w_{AB}(a,b)+w_{BC}(b,c)+w_{AC}(a,c)=0$; Lop-AE-SparseTri is Definition 13 of Alman and Vassilevska Williams. "Solved in time $T$" refers to programs of the library's light language, which compiles to the word RAM: one program solves every instance within the bound, with a polynomially bounded need of memory and word size.
--
--   The exponent comes from Theorem 17 for the all-edges host at the middle dimension with $D=\lfloor n^{13/228}\rfloor$ and $g=\lceil D^{11/300}\rceil$: the oracle is called at inner dimension about $D^{289/300}\approx n^{0.0549}$, inside the regime $D^{91}\le n^5$, and $\tfrac{143}{68400}=\tfrac{11}{300}\cdot\tfrac{13}{228}$. This bound is what the reduction from APSP to all-edges Exact Triangle consumes.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The statement is `Claim.LopDetectP aeModel → Claim.ExactTriangleUniform aeModel (143 / 68400) 2`, where `ExactTriangleUniform M δ e` says `M.exactTriangle (uniformTime K δ e)` for some `K ≥ 1`, and `aeModel` reads "Exact Triangle" as the all-edges task.
-- source:
--   Developed for the prove2.me APSP exponent campaign (https://prove2.me/campaigns/apsp-exponent) on top of the Lean formalization anthropics/formal-math, folder 3sum-apsp, commit e1a4e65 (https://github.com/anthropics/formal-math/tree/e1a4e6508154ea59f030480661590a9fe3018011/3sum-apsp; Lean v4.33.1, Mathlib v4.33.1). The statement comes from the file 3sum-apsp/ThreeSumApsp/AllEdges/Theorem19Mid.lean of the campaign's modified copy of that library, which is not published; the new and modified definitions it uses are in the platform definition bundles APSP299791_Defs1 to APSP299791_Defs5. It builds on J. Alman and V. Vassilevska Williams, "Truly Subquadratic 3SUM and Truly Subcubic APSP via Triangles in Sparse Lopsided Graphs", arXiv:2610.06783v1 (https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.06783v1), Theorems 17 and 19 (pp. 33-35). This result belongs to an improvement of the paper's bounds developed for this campaign and is not stated in the paper.

